---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeExplorer from '../components/CodeExplorer.astro';
import { capabilities, project, sourceUrl } from '../data/project';
---
<Base title="Features" description="Explore the language features available in Scarp v0.0.5-alpha.1, from bindings and typed functions to numerical values and source modules.">
  <section class="wrap page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The language today</p><h1>From small expressions<br />to bigger ideas.</h1><p class="lead">Available in v{project.version}. A working foundation, with room to evolve.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap section compact"><div class="feature-grid">{capabilities.map(item => <div class="feature"><span class="feature-number">{item.number}</span><h2>{item.title}</h2><p>{item.text}</p><a class="text-link" href={sourceUrl(item.link)}>{item.label} ↗</a></div>)}</div></section>
  <section class="wrap section learning-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read it. Run it. Explore it.</p><h2>A few lines<br />of Scarp.</h2><p class="section-description">Use <code>print</code> for output, <code>bind</code> for an immutable value, and <code>var</code> when a value needs to change. Typed functions use <code>funcra</code>.</p><a class="inline-link" href={project.docs + 'language/overview'}>Open the language guide ↗</a></div><CodeExplorer /></section>
  <section class="wrap section prose"><h2>More in the current interpreter</h2><ul><li>Lexical scopes, shadowing, short-circuit booleans, and <code>if</code>/<code>elif</code>/<code>else</code>.</li><li>Bounded <code>while</code> and <code>repeat</code> loops, plus <code>break</code> and <code>continue</code>.</li><li>Independent execution budgets and automatic retirement of inaccessible scope values.</li><li>Source diagnostics with error codes, locations, excerpts, and repair guidance.</li><li><code>run</code>, <code>check</code>, and <code>tokens</code> CLI commands, plus explicit Rust embedding APIs.</li></ul><h2>Know the boundaries</h2><p>Scarp currently interprets programs. Native code generation, a package manager, general-purpose collections, user-defined types, a general tensor engine, GPU execution, and automatic differentiation are future milestones. Execution budgets do not measure total process memory or form a security sandbox.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/development/">Read the full development status →</a></section>
</Base>
